<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ningyuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1626">1626</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ningyuan was fought in 1626 at Ningyuan, in modern Xingcheng in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, when the Ming commander Yuan Chonghuan defended the walled town against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nurhaci">Nurhaci</a>'s Later Jin army. Using Portuguese-style <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>, the defenders inflicted heavy losses and forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> to withdraw. It was Nurhaci's first serious defeat, and he died later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ningyuan.jpg" alt="Battle of Ningyuan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Ningyuan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
